					)
				)
			)
			(property "Note" "TI SLVS916I section 5 defines the DSJ package as 14 numbered pins plus ONE exposed thermal pad; TI gives PGND and the exposed thermal pad pin number '-' and states the exposed thermal pad is connected to PGND. Pin/pad 15 (PGND_EP) is the AQROOT/KiCad logical identifier for that unnumbered exposed PGND thermal pad; it is NOT a manufacturer package pin number. There is no pin 16 - an earlier model wrongly split the single thermal terminal into 15 PGND + 16 EP."
