				)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "SYMBOL CONFLICT RESOLVED (2026-08-07). This instance is now Switch:SW_SPDT with pins 1/2/3, matching the 3-terminal JS102011SAQN. Pole mapping VERIFIED 1:1 - KiCad pin 2 (name 'B') is the pole, sitting alone on the opposite side of the symbol body from throws 1 ('A') and 3 ('C'), and C&K terminal 2 is likewise the COMMON/POLE. Wiring as built: pin 2 = BQ25185_SYS (source), pin 1 = U12 EN + TP13, pin 3 = unused throw carrying a no_connect. Electrical intent is unchanged and still SPST-in-practice (VINA -> switch -> EN, never switching GND). Actuator direction and travel still require the enclosure mechanical review."
			(at 190.5 63.5 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Package" "Right-angle SMD SPDT slide switch, C&K JS series. FOOTPRINT VERIFIED against the C&K JS-series drawing (octopart mirror of the C&K/ITT datasheet), page 4 'RIGHT ANGLE SURFACE MOUNT / PCB MOUNT - HOLE LAYOUT' for JS102011SAQN. Verified exact: terminal pitch 2.5 TYP; two locating holes dia 0.9 with 6.8 span, i.e. x = +/-3.4; three SPDT lands; body 9.0 x 3.6 + 2.0. Documented delta: KiCad land is 1.25 wide vs the drawing's 1.2 TYP, a 0.025 mm per-side solder-fillet allowance. Mechanically critical features (hole diameter, hole span, pitch) match exactly. Contact rating 6 VDC 0.3 A, 5000 cycles. Pole mapping unchanged and previously verified 1:1: KiCad pin 2 = C&K terminal 2 = COMMON."
			(at 190.5 63.5 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
