	(text "=== B. AUTONOMOUS DEAD-CELL RECOVERY (Candidate B, D-065) - USB-POWERED, FIRMWARE-INDEPENDENT ==="
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 325.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f4b9455b-5861-3edf-ef90-20e48945f59f")
	)
	(text "Ratiometric polarity bridge (trip at V_BAT = 0, supply-independent) + handoff comparator + LTC4368 FAULT = hardware 3-input AND. Matched Schottkys D10/D11 keep the bridge ratiometric AND block battery drain when USB is absent."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 329.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "04dbb653-2871-9b7b-6b84-f467c49fc137")
	)
	(text "Q6/Q7/Q8 in series form the AND. Q9 inverts FAULT (active-low) so FAULT-ASSERTED becomes a positive enable. Recovery current = (VBUS - Vf) / R95; single-fault ceiling into a reversed cell = (VBUS - Vf + 4.2) / R95.\nR95 = 560R LOCKED (P-20, D-105): 8.4 mA nominal at VBUS 5.0 V into a 0 V pack (7.9-8.9 mA over 4.75-5.25 V), inside the accepted 5-10 mA band. Single-fault ceiling rises to 15.9 mA nominal / 16.6 mA worst case - B-27 restated, still ~0.007 C."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 332.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "35a21e95-2d21-f0b0-fb20-86c5d4c632d6")
	)
